    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia**_\n\n## Summary\n- `tools/devonthink-to-litdb.py`: indexes the highlighted pages of DEVONthink PDFs in litdb (one row per highlighted page, source = the record's item address with `?page=N`, incremental, `--dry-run` first).\n- `tools/litdb-query.py`: a search process that keeps litdb's model loaded (words, meaning, or both).\n- `sp-litdb` (`C-c k l`, index with `C-c k I`): searches it from Emacs. Hits are `key p. N` candidates of the category `sp-litdb`; Embark actions open the page in DEVONthink, insert a link or `[cite:@key p. N]`, or collect hits with their highlights into a note. Documented as the complement to `org-semantic` (what you wrote) and DEVONthink's own search (every PDF).\n\nFollows #209 (design) and #210 (`ROAM_REFS`).\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] 5 ERT tests in Emacs 31.1 batch (`tests/sp-litdb-test.el`).\n- [x] Indexer and search process run in the shell on one real record (8 rows; vector, fulltext and hybrid).\n- [x] Real search process driven through the Emacs code in batch.\n- [ ] Run the indexer with `--dry-run`, then for real; then `C-c k l`, `embark-collect`, and `n` in Emacs.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
